# The annotations of the game image: the single source of truth for src/game/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py).
# The format is in kit/mkgame.py, class Annotations (docs/ann-format.md). One line an entry:
#
#   @module NAME ; title            the entries from here on go to NAME.asm, the title heads the file
#   @about a paragraph              the module file's header text, one paragraph a line
#   $ADDR c Name ; title            a routine
#   > a description line
#   $ADDR b Name ; title            data (w words, t text, s space; "b Name 8" rows of 8)
#   @res graphics/NAME.bin          the entry is a resource: src/res/..., INCBIN
#   $ADDR Name ; comment            a label and comment inside an entry
#   @isub $ADDR LD HL,-6            the instruction written so
#   @equ $ADDR Name [N] ; comment   a variable past the image: an EQU, its operands by name
#   @inline $ADDR                   a routine that reads its data after the CALL
#
# Evidence: the recordings f1 (launch, flight, hyperspace), w1 (witch space, Thargoids), d1 (docked: the status,
# market, data and chart screens, the launch); "ran" counts below are their L1 instruction counts. What no
# recording reached is said to be known from the code only.


# Constants the bytes cannot tell from addresses (each was written as a code label plus an offset)
@isub $764A LD HL,$A000
@isub $7659 LD HL,$A000
@isub $7724 LD HL,$A000
@isub $7733 LD HL,$A000
@isub $8085 LD SP,BackBuffer+$1000
@isub $808E LD IX,$FF*$100
@isub $80A0 LD IX,$8000
@isub $80BE LD IX,$FF*$100
@isub $8142 LD SP,BackBuffer+$1000
@isub $8F83 LD HL,$FCCB
@isub $96AC LD DE,$C00C
@isub $9F20 LD DE,$8000
@isub $A4CC LD IY,ShipSlots-$27
@isub $A1CB LD HL,$7FFF
@isub $A1DB LD HL,$8000
@isub $B621 LD IX,ShipSlots-$27
@isub $B19C LD HL,$8040
@isub $B237 LD HL,$8040
@isub $B363 LD HL,$8040
@isub $D123 LD DE,$DF1F
@isub $D142 LD DE,$E017
@isub $EB03 LD HL,LaserItems-1
@isub $FE4B LD HL,$80FF
@isub $FEB9 LD HL,$8066
@module lowdata ; The low data: the scanner and dashboard save areas, the font, the ship slots and the ship blueprints
@about $5B00-$6047 is TZX block 37 (03-build-and-load.md 3.7); $6048 on is the first decrypted chunk. Nothing here runs.
@about The 3D view is the top two thirds of the screen, drawn into the back buffer at $C000 and copied to $4000 (CopyBackBuffer $7FBE); the dashboard is the bottom third. ScannerSave and DashAttrSave hold copies of dashboard parts the views paint over.

$5B00 b ScannerSave 13 ; The scanner's background: 48 pixel lines of 13 bytes, $5049-$5055 on of the screen's bottom third
> ScannerCopy $990C copies 13 bytes a line, 8 lines a row, 6 rows between the screen ($5049, the scanner ellipse of the dashboard) and here. ScannerSaveMode $98A2 patches it to save the screen here (EX DE,HL, PUSH HL / POP HL in place of NOP, PUSH DE / POP DE), ScannerClear $98CD back to restore it every frame (f1: 554 runs). DashboardSave $817E also copies the dashboard's attributes ($5A00-$5AFF) to $5B00, and DashboardRestore $8042 copies them back.
> The image's bytes are what the last copy left: attribute bytes ($07, $17) in the first page, then the mastering machine's system variables (03 3.10) to $5D6F.
$5C00 ; from here the bytes are TZX block 37's copy of the mastering machine's system variables (03-build-and-load.md 3.10)
$5D70 b Font 8 ; The character set: 91 glyphs of 8 bytes for the codes $20-$7A, read by PrintChar $D499
> Codes $20-$7A, 8 bytes a glyph top line first. Most are ASCII letters, digits and signs; the codes $21-$26, $2B and $3B-$3E (! " # and so on) are the dashboard's frame pieces (slants, corners, bars), drawn by the same printer.
@res fonts/font.bin
$6048 b ShipSlots 39 ; The 8 ship slots, 39 bytes each: the objects in space
> Eight records of $27 bytes from $6048 (slot n at $6048 + 39 n), read and written by every ship routine (UpdateShips $9CBB walks them). The record: +$00-$08 the position x, y, z (3 bytes each, sign in bit 7 of the top byte), +$09-$1A the orientation vectors, +$1B the speed, +$20 / +$21 the flags, +$22 the energy, +$23 / +$24 the blueprint address, +$25 / +$26 the AI state (07-objects.md). The image's bytes are leftovers of a BASIC program in the developer's memory (" ***---", "3000"), overwritten when a game starts.
$6159 b Slot7 39 ; Slot 7, the last of the eight: the player's missile in flight, the turning ship on the title. The code names it directly (TurnTitleShip, ActionTitleShip, the hostility test of UpdateSlot); it is no work copy: the ship routines work on each slot in place
$6180 b Blueprints 4 ; The blueprint table: 19 entries of $C3, the blueprint address and its class
> CreateShip $B898 reads entry A AND $3F (HL = $6180 + 4 A + 1): the word is the blueprint. The first byte of each is $C3 (a JP opcode; nothing jumps here). The last byte is the class the spawn code picks ships by: 0 the station and the missile, 1 debris (pod, plate, canister, splinter, asteroid), 2 traders (rock hermit, Viper, the trader Cobra and Python), 3 pirates and Thargoids, 4 the Sidewinder, Krait and Thargon (07-objects.md).
$61CC b ShipAsp 23 ; blueprint 13: the header (19 vertices, 28 edges, 12 faces)
@res ships/ships.bin
