@module startup ; The vectors, the flight variables, the start, the pause menu and the title
@about The game's code starts at $6FF2 with a few jump vectors other parts call by address, the variables the flight loop shares (the view, the control rates, the dashboard bar values, the planet and the sun), the pause menu and the title screen. Start $70E0 is where the kickoff enters (JP $70E0, 03-build-and-load.md 3.7).

$6FF2 c EnergyBombVector ; JP EnergyBomb (FlightLoop calls it every frame)
$6FF5 c FlashVector ; JP FlashScreen (known from the code only: no caller ran)
$6FF8 c FillAttrsVector ; JP FillAttrs
$6FFB b ChartIcons 8 ; The four sizes of a system's dot on the local chart, 8x8 each
> DrawChartIcon $ED27 picks one (DE = $6FFB + 8 n) and ORs it onto the chart.
$701B b Commodities 4 ; The 17 commodities: 4 bytes each, the market generator's table
> MakeMarket $E148 (d1: the Lave market) reads the 68 bytes from $701B: the base price, the economy factor (bit 7 its sign) with the unit in its top bits, the base quantity and the fluctuation mask (10-gameplay-logic.md). Firearms is entry 11: ZeroFirearms $B7AC zeroes its price when the special cargo mission needs it.
$705F b EquipmentPrices 3 ; The prices of the equipment the Equip screen sells
> Read by EquipShip $E973 through EquipPricePtr $EB2F (t1 bought a missile at frame 1474: EquipShip 1 run). The fuel price at $7060 is written by the hyperspace code ($DC66, $DCAA).
$7089 c EnergyBomb ; Detonate the energy bomb when its key is down and one is fitted
> Every frame (f1, w1, d1: 1076 runs) from FlightLoop through EnergyBombVector. KeyCombat $FC0B bit 5 is the bomb key; EnergyBombFitted $D08A non-zero is a bomb on board. The bomb is used up, BombKill $9C95 = 1 makes UpdateShips destroy what it can, sound 0 is requested and the screen flashes 24 times (FlashScreen). k2 fired one at frame 3304 (FlashScreen 24 runs; the Thargoids unhurt), m1 and m2 one each.
$70A2 EnergyBombFlash
$70A9 c FlashScreen ; One flash: the 3D view's attributes $28, then $0F
$70B0 c FillAttrs ; Fill the 3D view's attributes ($5800-$59FF) with L after the next interrupt
> L is the attribute; with CloakOn $D041 zero only its INK bits stay (AND 7). The entry FillAttrsTinted $70BA skips that step; with NovaMission $D081 set the attribute is ANDed with $3A. After a HALT the stack pointer is put at $59FF and 16 rows of 15 PUSHes write the 512 bytes; FillSP keeps the real SP.
$70BA FillAttrsTinted
$70C4 FillAttrsNow
$70CF FillAttrsRow
$70D1 FillAttrsPush
$70DE w FillSP ; FillAttrs' saved stack pointer
$70E0 c Start ; The game's entry from the kickoff: JP Title
$70E3 b ViewIndex ; The view: 0-3 the space views (front, rear, left, right), 4 and up the screens
> SelectView $80D3 sets it from the keys; below 4 the flight loop draws space, from 4 a status, market or chart screen is up (7 and 8 the charts: ChartCursorKeys $71F3).
$70E4 b RollRate ; The roll rate this frame (bit 7 the sign), copied from the high byte of RollControl ($FF09)
$70E5 b PitchRate ; The pitch rate this frame, from the high byte of PitchControl ($FF0B)
$70E6 b SpeedRate ; The speed this frame, from the high byte of SpeedControl ($FF0D)
$70E7 b BarDrawn ; The dashboard bars: 13 pairs of the length last drawn and the value, the fore shield first
> DrawBars $84D9 compares each value with the byte before it and draws only a changed bar; a value is 0-$A0, a quarter of it the length in pixels. The first 11 are solid bars (the shields, the fuel, the cabin and laser temperatures, the altitude, the speed, the four energy banks), the last two the roll and pitch markers. ResetDashboard $9946 starts the shields, the altitude and the banks at $A0.
$70E8 BarForeShield ; The fore shield
$70E9 ; the aft shield's last length
$70EA BarAftShield ; The aft shield
$70EC BarFuel ; The fuel
$70EE BarCabinTemp ; The cabin temperature (zero at a reset)
$70F0 BarLaserTemp ; The laser temperature
$70F2 BarAltitude ; The altitude above the planet
$70F4 BarSpeed ; The speed: SpeedRate * 5 + 5
$70F6 BarEnergy1 ; Energy bank 1
$70F8 BarEnergy2 ; Energy bank 2
$70FA BarEnergy3 ; Energy bank 3
$70FC BarEnergy4 ; Energy bank 4
$70FE BarRoll ; The roll marker: $15 +/- the roll rate
$7100 BarPitch ; The pitch marker: $15 +/- the pitch rate
$7101 ; spare
$7103 b WitchSpace ; Non-zero in witch space after a misjump (the hyperspace arrival, JumpArrive): no sun, no planet, no station, four stars, Thargoids
$7104 b Condition ; The condition light as an attribute: 0 docked, 4 green, 6 yellow, 2 red, $63 red flashing
> ConditionLight $99A4 writes it to the dashboard's attributes ($5A28, $5A48) every frame and sets 4 again for the next: the distance code makes it 6 near the planet or the sun and $63 very near ($82D7), a shield at zero makes it 2, and $63 alternates between 0 and 2 (ConditionFlash $99A3).
$7105 w StarSeed ; The stardust generator's seed (StarRandom $7E86)
$7107 b SunPosition 3 ; The sun's position: x, y, z, 3 bytes each (sign in bit 7 of the top byte)
> DashDistances $81A9 turns its distance into the cabin temperature (BarCabinTemp) and TooClose; DrawSunPlanet $7584 draws it first, as a filled circle.
$7110 b PlanetPosition 3 ; The planet's position: x, y, z
> DashDistances turns its distance into the altitude (BarAltitude, $A0 - distance) and the safe zone (SafeZone, all three coordinates below $0200).
$7119 c DrawChartCircleVector ; JP DrawChartCircle
$711C b SafeZone ; Non-zero inside the space station's safe zone: the planet's three coordinates below $0200
$711D b StationLaunch ; Non-zero while slot 0, the station, flies in after a launch
$711E b SunNear ; Non-zero when the sun's distance is below $2000 (DashDistances $81EC)
$711F b TooClose ; Non-zero when the ship has hit the planet or the sun
$7120 b SunLarge ; Non-zero when the sun's circle radius is $28 or more (DrawSunPlanet $75A8)
$7121 c ConditionLightVector ; JP ConditionLight
$7124 b HoldRates ; Non-zero: FlightLoop keeps the control rates of the frame before
$7125 c SoundTickVector ; JP SoundTick (the interrupt handler calls it)
$7128 b SoundRequests ; The sound requests: one bit a sound, set by the game, served by SoundTick
$7129 b AutoDocked ; 1 when the docking computer docked the ship (DockKeys $71AE)
$712A c AddDigitVector ; JP AddDigit (known from the code only, like the next two)
$712D c AttrFillVector ; JP DashAttrs $9974
$7130 c AddDigit ; (HL) = (HL) * 10 + B: one typed digit into a number
$713C c CopyRates ; Copy the control rates the interrupt built to this frame's rates and the indicators
> Every pass of FlightLoop (197283 runs over f1, w1, d1). The high bytes of RollControl, PitchControl and SpeedControl ($FF09, $FF0B, $FF0D) are what ReadControls $FE01 accumulated in the interrupt: copied to RollRate, PitchRate and SpeedRate; the roll and pitch indicators get $15 plus or minus the rate (a sign-magnitude byte), the speed indicator 5 * speed + 5.
$714B CopyRatesRollNeg
$7151 CopyRatesRollBar
$7162 CopyRatesPitchNeg
$7168 CopyRatesPitchBar
$717B c DockKeys ; Dock: after the collision code docked the ship, or on the docking computer key in the safe zone
> Docked $9C9A is set by the collision code when the ship enters the station ($B591) and by the arrival code ($9466): cleared, and the docking sequence runs. Otherwise KeyCombat $FC0B bit 7 (the docking computer key, cleared here) docks when the ship is in the safe zone, DockingComputer $D08C is fitted, Condition is not 0, $D03F is 0 and slot 0's flag bit 2 is clear; AutoDocked is set. Then the front view, the dashboard, CentreMarkers and the docking scene (SceneDock $93ED). f1 and w1: 863 runs, no dock.
$7187 DockKeysComputer
$71B3 DockKeysDock
$71BA DockKeysCentre
$71C0 c CentreMarkers ; Move the sun and the planet half way to slot 0's position (known from the code only)
$71CE CentreMarker
$71D6 CentreMarkerStore
$71E4 c HalfDifference ; HL = half the difference between a marker coordinate (IY) and the slot's (IX)
$71F3 c ChartCursorKeys ; On the charts (ViewIndex 7, 8): a cursor key moves the cursor through the chart vector
$7210 ChartCursorBit
$7221 b CloakKeyCount ; Counts the frames down to the next look at the cloak key (every second frame)
$7222 c CloakKey ; Every second frame: Y (KeyScreens $FC08 bit 7) switches the cloaking device on or off once the mission has given it
> The device is MissionFlags bit 6 (AddCargoSpecial, the mission ship's canister). On: CloakOn = 1 while energy bank 3 ($70FA) is $28 or more, the station's hostile bit cleared, AllHostile 0 and the view's attributes $0F (blue paper: FillAttrs keeps the paper while CloakOn is set); off: attributes 7. With bank 3 below $28 the decrement leaves CloakOn at $FF, on but untinted (known from the code only). 1076 runs, the key never pressed with the device (no recording earned it, CloakOn 0 runs): the rest is known from the code only.
$7253 CloakTint
$7257 CloakPlain
$7259 CloakFill
$725C c NovaTint ; After the dashboard is redrawn (ClearView): the nova's red tint (attributes 2) again while NovaMission is set
$7260 NovaTintFill
$7265 c CloakRestore ; After the dashboard is redrawn: the cloak's tint ($0F) again while CloakOn is set
$726C c NovaSunGrows ; At the launch (SceneLaunch): in the nova's system the sun starts to grow (SunGrows 1) and the view turns red
$7278 c ArrivalScreens ; At the dock: the mission page MissionState asks for: 1 or 2 the briefing (MissionQuestion), 5 the award (MissionDone), 6 SHIP BOARDED BY THARGONS and the title
> No code sets state 6: the Thargon boarding is unreachable (known from the code only). The routine ran at each dock: dk 2, gx 1, m1 2, m2 1 (the briefing, MissionQuestion, at frame 2926).
$727F ArrivalScreensFirst
$728D c PirateStation ; At the dock: a station whose roll counter's bit 7 is clear is pirate-held: SHIP BOARDED BY PIRATES, THEY SHOW NO MERCY, the title
> TitleNext sets bit 7 of slot 0's +$1D (the station's roll counter, bit 7 the direction); an arrival clears it with a chance that grows as the government falls (JumpArrive), so the station spins the other way: the only warning. Known from the code only.
$7295 BackToTitleMessage
$72A2 b ControlMethod ; The control method chosen on the title: 1 Kempston (left on port $1F, bit 5 clear), 2 Cursor (5 held), 3 Sinclair (6 held)
$72A3 c PauseMenu ; The pause: hold the game while the key's bit is set and run the option keys
> KeyViews $FC0A bit 7 is the pause key (the keyboard scan sets it). The game waits for the key to be released, then reads keys until SPACE (resume) or 1 (back to the title, carry set): B reverse the joystick, D keyboard damping, F the option bit 6, K keyboard / joystick, Q sound off, R recentring, S sound on, Y the Y axis reversed; an unknown key beeps (ErrorBeep). Each toggles a bit of Options $FC0E (HL = $FC0E). w1 paused once and pressed F and SPACE.
$72AC PauseRelease
$72B3 PauseKey
$72F1 c ClearKeys ; Zero the five key bytes $FC08-$FC0C
$72FF PauseQuit
$7304 c OptionReverse ; Key B: Options bit 4
$730A c OptionDamping ; Key D: Options bit 3
$7310 c OptionBit6 ; Key F: Options bit 6
$7316 c OptionSoundOff ; Key Q: Options bit 7 off
$731C c OptionRecentre ; Key R: Options bit 2
$7322 c OptionSoundOn ; Key S: Options bit 7 on, and the sound requests cleared
$732B c OptionReverseY ; Key Y: Options bit 5
$7331 c OptionKeyboard ; Key K: between the keyboard and the control method chosen on the title
$733D OptionKeyboardSwap
$7342 OptionKeyboardDone
$7344 c ErrorBeep ; A short beep: 6 frames of 4 rising tones on the speaker
$7348 ErrorBeepFrame
$734C ErrorBeepTone
$7356 ErrorBeepHigh
$735D ErrorBeepLow
$7366 c Title ; The title: the rotating ship, "Load new commander", then the control method
> SP is kept in TitleSP $7578 for the game overs (PirateStation, ArrivalScreens). The ship action $79 (DoShipAction $9C9C) places the title Cobra; then the title loop draws it each frame (DrawTitleShip $9CAF) until a key: Y (KeyCode $FC0D + 1 = $5A) opens the commander load menu (CommanderMenuVector $D04E). The second loop shows "PRESS SPACE, COMMANDER" with the next title ship each pass (TitleShipCount) and reads a joystick held left (Kempston: port $1F bit 1 with bit 5 clear; Cursor: 5, KeyDigits bit 1; Sinclair: 6, KeyDigits bit 3) or SPACE (the keyboard); then the new game (NewGameVector $D033) and FlightLoop. c1, f1, w1 and d1 all start here (d1 at frame 784 of w1's title loop).
$7370 TitleShip
$7378 TitleLoad
$7394 TitleIfNotZero
$739E TitleNext
$73BA TitleIfNotBelow
$73C3 TitleLoop
$73E2 TitleKeys
$73F4 TitleKeyboard
$73F7 TitleMethod
$73FD TitleStart
$7426 c TitleTextLoad ; The title text and "LOAD NEW COMMANDER (Y/N)?" (other token 6, row 14, column 1)
$7430 c TitleTextPress ; The title text and "PRESS SPACE, COMMANDER" (other token 7, row 14, column 4)
$7438 TitleTextPrint
$7447 c TitleElite ; "---- E L I T E ----" (code $1D: token $8F) at row 1, column 5, in the title colours
$7459 c PlainText ; Clear the title-colour bit the two title texts set
$7461 c WhiteAttrs ; The attributes of the top two thirds: white INK on black
$7467 c FillAttrPage ; 256 attributes $07 from HL
$746B FillAttrPageLoop
$7470 b TitleShipCount ; The title ship counter: the next title ship's blueprint
@module flightloop ; The flight loop, the sun and the planet on screen, the division
@about FlightLoop $7471 is the game's main loop from the title on: one pass every 5 to 6.5 frames in space, the same loop (with the screens) when docked or on a status screen. The sun and the planet are circles: their positions (SunPosition $7107, PlanetPosition $7110) are projected for the current view and drawn by the circle code (06-rendering.md).

$7471 c FlightLoop ; The main loop: the controls, the view, the pause, the jump keys, the ships, the screen
> A pass: CopyRates (unless HoldRates), SelectView, PauseMenu (1 there goes back to the title), JumpKeysVector $D042. Docked (Condition 0) it only reads the chart cursor and the menu key (KeySteer $FC09 bit 5: the commander load / save menu, CommanderMenuVector $D04E); in flight it runs DockKeys, the debug key ($7EDE), the sun and planet rotation, the station run-in, then for a space view: the dashboard, the 3D view cleared (ClearView $8080), the sun and the planet, the stardust, the screen texts, the ships (ShipsVector $9C80), the effects, the back buffer copied to the screen (CopyBackBuffer $7FBE), the debris, the bars, the flash, the dashboard keys and DashDistances. f1, w1, d1: 197283 passes. In space a pass takes 5.0 (no ships) to 6.5 frames (four Thargoids), its only wait the HALT in CloakKey every second pass; docked it spins with no HALT, about 91 passes a frame (d1 600-700: 9118 in 100 frames; runtime-analysis.md).
> TooClose set (the ship hit the sun or the planet, or a fatal hit) ends the game: 30 frames of other token 9 over the stardust, 50 frames' pause, then the title ($739E).
