@module backbuffer ; The back buffer, the dashboard save and restore, the choice of view or screen
@about The 3D view (the top 128 lines) is drawn into the back buffer $C000-$CFFF, laid out like the screen's top two thirds, and copied to $4000-$4FFF once a frame (CopyBackBuffer). The dashboard (the bottom third and its attributes) is saved before a full-screen page and put back after (DashboardSave, DashboardRestore).
@about The keys 1-4 and ENTER, L, K, P, O, I pick what is shown (SelectView): in flight 1-4 are the front, rear, left and right views; docked 1 launches and 2-4 are the buy, sell and equip screens; the six letters are the screens of the table at $D000 (ScreenTable).

$7FBE c CopyBackBuffer ; Copy the back buffer $C000-$CFFF to the screen's top two thirds
> Four CopyThird calls of 1024 bytes: the even pixel lines of the top third ($4000), the even lines of the middle third ($4800), then the odd lines of both ($4100, $4900). The buffer address is the screen address with bit 15 set. It runs 1830 times in f1, w1, d1.
$7FE3 c CopyThird ; Copy every other pixel line of one third: 8 character rows of 4 lines of 32 LDI
$7FE5 CopyThirdRow
$7FEA CopyThirdLine
$8042 c DashboardRestore ; Put the dashboard back if a full-screen page wiped it (the top-left byte reads $FF)
> The screen byte $4000 is $FF only while a full page is up (ClearScreen draws the frame). Then: SoundOff $94FE, the page cleared (ClearScreenVector $D036), the side attributes of the top two thirds zeroed (columns 0 and 31), the dashboard's pixels from DashSave $C000 and its attributes from $5B00, the tints again, and the scanner put in save mode (ScannerSaveMode $98A2).
$804B DashboardRestoreNow
$8059 DashboardRestoreLoop
$8080 c ClearView ; Clear the back buffer with the view's frame: lines 0 and 127 solid, a pixel at each side
> With interrupts off and SP at $D000 it PUSHes 4096 bytes: the bottom line $FF, 126 lines of $01 ... $80 (the side pixels), the top line $FF. f1, w1, d1: 1827 runs.
$8098 ClearViewBottom
$80A6 ClearViewLine
$80C5 ClearViewTop
$80D1 w ClearViewSP ; ClearView's and CallScreen's saved stack pointer
$80D3 c SelectView ; Change the view or the screen on the keys 1-4, ENTER, L, K, P, O, I
> KeyViews $FC0A bits 0-3 are 1-4: in flight the views 0-3 (SetView); docked key 1 is the launch (SceneLaunch $93ED) and 2-4 the screens 4-6 (CallScreen). KeyScreens $FC08 bits 5 to 0 are I, O, P, K, L and ENTER: the screens 7-12. Nothing while TunnelLoop $D040 is set. The keys are cleared after (SelectViewDone).
