@module dashboard ; The dashboard: the distances to the sun and the planet, the compass, the bars
@about DashDistances $81A9 runs once a frame in flight: it measures the sun (the cabin temperature, TooClose), the planet (the altitude, the safe zone) and points the compass at the planet, or at the station inside the safe zone. DrawBars $84D9 redraws the 13 bars whose value changed.

$81A3 b DashWork 6 ; DashDistances' results: SunClose, PlanetClose, the compass x and y offsets, the compass behind flag
$81A4 SunClose ; 1 when the sun's coordinates are all below $0100 (its distance was measured)
$81A5 PlanetClose ; 1 when the planet's are all below $0200
$81A6 CompassX ; The compass dot's x offset (bit 7 the sign)
$81A7 CompassY ; The compass dot's y offset
$81A8 CompassBehind ; 1 when the target is behind (z negative): the hollow dot
$81A9 c DashDistances ; The sun's and the planet's distances on the bars, the safe zone, the compass
> The sun: with all three top bytes clear its distance (VectorLength) gives the cabin temperature (BarCabinTemp, through DistanceBand) and below $2000 SunNear; a distance below $4000 in the other test sets TooClose ($82D1). The planet: below $0200 on all axes its distance gives the altitude ($A0 minus it, below $4000 TooClose) and SafeZone. The compass points at the planet, or at slot 0 (the station) when SafeZone is set and StationLaunch is not $FF: each of x and y divided by the distance (CompassDivide) times 8, the sign kept; then DrawCompass. f1, w1, d1: 1076 runs.
