@module circles ; The circles: the sun filled, the planet outlined, the chart's range circle, the hit flashes
@about One circle engine draws every circle: the centre in CircleX $861B and CircleY $861A (offsets from the view's centre, the signs in CircleQuadrant $861C bits 0 and 1), the radius in CircleRadius $861D. CircleMode $8629 is 0 for a filled circle (the sun: DrawCircleDI), 1 for an outline (the planet: DrawCircle). A radius below 9 is not drawn.
@about DrawCircleShape $86EE turns the centre into screen coordinates and sorts the circle by how it meets the view's edges: wholly inside (four arcs, CircleArcs $87C8), or cut by the top, the bottom or the sides (the clipped fillers $87FE-$893F). Each row's half width comes from the table of squares at $BE00 (HalfChord $8ACD); the outline is stepped like a Bresenham circle in the alternate registers, the fill writes whole bytes by PUSHing $FFFF into the row (a JR patched into one of six chains of 16 PUSH AF, FillSpan1-6).
@about The code draws into the back buffer: page $C0 and 128 lines. DrawChartCircle $8E29 patches 32 bytes of it (the addresses at CirclePatchSites) for the chart screens on $4000 and puts them back after; HitFlash $8F0D patches the base (CircleBase) to draw on the real screen too.

$8619 b CircleZero ; One byte no code reads (known from the code only)
$861A b CircleY ; The centre's offset from the view's centre, down or up by CircleQuadrant bit 1
$861B b CircleX ; The centre's offset across, by bit 0
$861C b CircleQuadrant ; Bit 0 x positive (right), bit 1 y positive (up), bits 2 and 3 the centre off the view across or down
$861D b CircleRadius ; The radius in pixels (9 and more drawn)
$861E b CircleRowOffset ; DrawCircleShape's working copy of CircleY, clipped to the edge it meets
$861F b CircleColOffset ; Its copy of CircleX
$8620 b CircleScreenY ; The centre's row: 64 - or + CircleY
$8621 b CircleScreenX ; The centre's column: 128 + or - CircleX
$8622 b ClipHalfWidth ; The half width of the circle at the clipping row (HalfChord)
$8623 w CircleSP ; The stack pointer saved while the fills PUSH and the chart patches POP
$8625 w HalfChordTarget ; HalfChord's radius² - row²
$8627 b CirclePointX ; PointRight's x
$8628 b RunRight ; 1 while the run being plotted grows x (the right half), 0 while it shrinks x; the fills read it to pick the edge test
$8629 b CircleMode ; 0 a filled circle (the sun), 1 an outline (the planet)
$862A b ChartPatchCount ; The 32 bytes DrawChartCircle patches and puts back

$862B c OutlineRunUpRight ; Plot an outline run: up the screen, x growing (the alternate registers step it)
$8643 c OutlineRunUpLeft ; Plot an outline run: up the screen, x shrinking
