@module tunnel ; The ring tunnel of the launch, the dock and the hyperspace jump; the launch and dock sequences
@about The tunnel is a row of concentric outlined circles at the view's centre ($0F, $0000 in the circle's variables). Each ring has a distance that one frame takes one from; its radius is 256 / distance (TunnelDivide) and only a ring of radius 4 or more is drawn, so the rings come out of the centre and grow to the edge. Two flags at $D03F: TunnelOn (a launch or dock tunnel is running) and TunnelLoop ($D040, the frames run inside one call). The launch, the dock and the jump patch three bytes of TunnelFrame for their shape: the jump of JR Z at $9317 (its own loop or one frame a call), the last frame (CP at $9325) and where the loop ends (JR C at $932A).

$928C c TunnelFrameText ; The view's texts (ViewTexts), then a tunnel frame while TunnelOn is set
> The flight loop's and the scenes' per-frame call. 1220 runs over f1, w1, d1.
$9296 c TunnelStart ; Start the hyperspace tunnel when TunnelLoop is set: the controls and the ships reset, 16 rings
> In witch space (WitchSpace non-zero) slot 0's energy is cleared and ship action 1 runs first. Then the view cleared, TunnelTop $42, the jump sound (SoundJump), the 16 rings of TunnelRings, the last frame at 1 and the end at TunnelStop: $42 frames in one call. 2 runs (the jumps of f1 and w1).
$92B3 TunnelStartRings
$92D6 c TunnelFrame ; Draw the tunnel: every ring one step nearer, then show the frame
> With TunnelLoop set (the jump, the first frames of the launch and the dock) the frames loop here until TunnelTop passes the last frame; without it each call draws one frame and TunnelCount counts it.
$92E3 TunnelFrameLoop
$92E8 TunnelFrameRings
$92F9 TunnelFrameStart ; the ring table (patched: TunnelRings or LaunchRings)
$92FC TunnelFrameRing
$9313 TunnelFrameNext ; the JR Z's offset at $9318 is patched: $05 the loop, $1E one frame a call
$931E TunnelFrameShow ; the CP's value at $9326 (the last frame) and the JR C's offset at $932B (the end) are patched
$9337 c TunnelCount ; One frame of a tunnel drawn a frame a call: TunnelEnd when TunnelTop reaches 0
$9341 c TunnelStop ; The jump's tunnel over: both flags off, the 16 rings moved back by $BE, the view cleared and shown
$934E TunnelStopRings
$935E c TunnelOver ; The launch's first frames over: TunnelLoop off, the stardust made again
$9364 c TunnelOff ; The dock's first frames over: TunnelLoop off (reached by a jump: dk, gx, m1, m2 docked)
$9369 c TunnelEnd ; TunnelOn off and the 8 launch rings moved back by $C0 for the next time
$9373 TunnelEndRings
$937B c StarsRenew ; Make all 16 dots again ahead of the ship (StarRespawnFront patched for it), speed 7
> StarRespawnFront's two range bytes become $83 (from $BF and $9F) and the RET at its tail ($7E0E) replaces the JP, so each call places one dot from StarSeed; the bytes go back after the 16 dots.
$9395 StarsRenewDot
$93AC c TunnelDivide ; C = A * 256 / B (A < B): a ring's radius from its distance
> A restoring division, eight bits of quotient; C starts at $FE so the carry out of RL C after eight bits ends it. 3648 runs.
$93AE TunnelDivideLoop
$93B9 TunnelDivideSub
$93C0 c TunnelDone ; After the jump: the attributes white unless in the nova system (NovaMission $D081), LastSunRadius 0, the arrival sound
$93D0 b TunnelRingCount ; The number of rings (16 for the jump, 8 for the launch and the dock)
$93D1 b TunnelRingsLeft
$93D2 b TunnelTop ; The frames left
$93D3 b TunnelRings 8 ; The 16 ring distances of the jump tunnel, 2.5 apart
$93E3 b LaunchRings 8 ; The 8 ring distances of the launch and dock tunnel, and two spare bytes
$93ED c SceneLaunch ; The launch from the station (Condition 0) or the dock (in flight), with the tunnel
> Both: the 8 launch rings, TunnelTop $40, the last frame $30, TunnelOn and TunnelLoop set.
> The launch (d1 at Lave, 3 runs over f1, w1, d1): Condition green, the views reset, the dashboard drawn and reset (ResetFlight $9946), the planet ahead ($80 at z+1 of PlanetPosition, the sun's sign flipped), slot 0 the station just behind the ship (z = -$F0, its three axes the unit ones, $7F) with energy $F0, the bars, 16 frames in the first call (TunnelOver), 36 frames of the tunnel over the stardust and 11 with the sun and the planet.
> The dock (dk docked by hand at frame 2190 and by the computer at 3408; gx, m1, m2 docked too): speed $0C, no roll or pitch, the controls held, the first call's frames end at TunnelOff, then 47 frames, Condition docked, the dashboard saved, the controls cleared, the mission screens (ArrivalScreens), PirateStation and the status screen (CallScreen 7).
$9413 SceneDock
$9438 SceneDockFrame
$945D SceneLaunchNow
$94C8 SceneLaunchTunnel
