@module sound ; The beeper: the effects of the scenes, the background requests and the three generators
@about The beeper is driven from the frame interrupt: IM2Handler calls SoundTick $9579 (through SoundTickVector $7125) once a frame (13398 runs), and each call plays one slice of the current effect inside the interrupt, so an effect sounds while the main loop waits; a long slice (the laser's sweep) holds the main loop for most of a frame (runtime-analysis.md 8). SoundRequests $7128 holds one bit per wanted effect (bit 0 the energy bomb, 1 the missile, 2 an explosion, 3 a ship hit by the laser, 4 the laser, 5 the ECM, 6 the player hit); SoundTick takes the lowest bit, arms its generator through SoundTable and clears the bit when the effect ends. SoundMode $9522 is the generator: 1 a sweep, 2 noise read from the ROM, 3 a pulse train; bit 7 adds a second phase. The three scene sounds (the launch, the jump, the arrival) instead play their whole effect at once with the interrupts off (SoundPlay); Game Over's (SoundGameOver) goes through SoundPlay with the interrupts on.
@about Options bit 7 ($FC0E) is the sound switch: the pause menu's S turns it on (and clears the requests), Q off; every entry point returns at once when it is clear.

$9509 c ClearShips ; The station not hostile (+$21 bit 2) and slots 1-7 free (energy +$22 zero), ShipCount 0
> Run by the launch and the jump: no ship survives them.
$951A ClearShipsLoop
$9522 b SoundMode ; The generator playing: 0 none, 1 sweep, 2 noise, 3 pulses; bit 7 a second phase
$9523 w SoundPitch ; E: the passes left, D: the pitch (the delay count)
$9525 w SoundSource ; The pulse and noise generators read their levels from this address (the ROM)
$9527 c SoundLaunch ; The launch's and the dock's whistle: a pulse train played at once
> Called by the launch (SceneLaunchNow, as the tunnel starts), the dock (after SceneDock's frames) and GameOver: 4 runs, the launches of f1, w1 and d1 and the death of w1.
$9532 c SoundArrive ; The arrival from the jump (TunnelDone): a pulse train played at once
$953D c SoundJump ; The jump's start (TunnelStart): a pulse train played at once
$9548 c SoundGameOver ; Game Over's sound: SoundSecond's 160-level phase, played by SoundPlay with the interrupts on (1 run, the death of w1)
> The interrupt's SoundTick plays slices of the same effect while SoundPlay loops, and arms the explosion ShipsWreck requested in between. As SoundTick never set SoundBit for this effect, its SoundEnd flips the stale bit of the effect before (w1 frame 4308: the laser's bit 4 set again, SoundRequests $14); SoundPlay clears every request when it ends, so nothing is heard of it.
$9551 c SoundPlay ; Play the armed effect to its end (the scene sounds have the interrupts off), then clear the requests and EI
$955C SoundPlayDone
$9561 c SoundBomb ; SoundTable, bit 0: the energy bomb, falling pulses
> SoundTable is eight JPs, one per request bit; SoundTick computes the bit's number * 3. Bits 0, 1, 3 and 5 were set first in k2 (the bomb, the missile, a ship hit, the E.C.M.: SoundArmBomb, SoundArmMissile, SoundArmShipHit, SoundArmECM); bit 7 is never set and shares bit 6's code.
$9564 c SoundMissile ; SoundTable, bit 1: the missile launch, pulses
$9567 c SoundExplode ; SoundTable, bit 2: an explosion, two-phase pulses
$956A c SoundShipHit ; SoundTable, bit 3: a ship hit, noise
$956D c SoundLaser ; SoundTable, bit 4: the laser, a sweep
$9570 c SoundECM ; SoundTable, bit 5: the ECM, a sweep
$9573 c SoundHit ; SoundTable, bit 6: the player hit, noise
$9576 c SoundSpare ; SoundTable, bit 7: as bit 6 (never requested)
$9579 c SoundTick ; One slice of the effect playing, or arm the effect of the lowest request bit
> Runs once a frame from IM2Handler; with SoundMode 0 and no request it returns at once. The jump to SoundTable is computed (bit number * 3 + $9561), so the static walk does not see it.
$958C SoundTickBit
$959E SoundTickJump
$959F SoundTickMode
$95A6 c SoundPulses ; The pulse generator: 64 beeper levels from SoundSource, each held D loops; the pitch steps per pass
> The level is bit 3 or bit 4 of the ROM byte (the MIC and EAR bits of $FE), so the ROM's bytes give a rough waveform. The step added to D per pass is patched at $95BD and the 64 at $95AE. When E reaches 0: a second phase (bit 7, SoundSecond) or the end (SoundEnd).
$95AD SoundPulsesNow
$95AF SoundPulsesLoop
$95B5 SoundPulsesDelay
$95BB SoundPulsesPass
$95CF c SoundSecond ; The second phase of a two-phase effect: 160 levels a pass, pitch $40, 2 passes
$95E7 c SoundNoise ; The noise generator: 100 pulses whose length is a ROM byte / 4 (or / 2 + 8), D passes
> SoundArmNoise patches the instruction at $95F2: SRL A ($CB $3F) for a ship hit, ADD A,$10 ($C6 $10) for the player hit, so the hit's pulses are longer. L steps through the ROM page in SoundSource.
$95EE SoundNoiseNow
$95F0 SoundNoiseLoop
$95FC SoundNoiseHigh
$9602 SoundNoiseLow
$9607 c SoundPassEnd ; One pass done: D (or E) one less, the state saved, the end at 0
$9610 c SoundEnd ; The effect over: SoundMode 0 and its request bit cleared
$961B SoundEndBit
$9624 c SoundSweep ; The sweep generator: 15 square cycles a pass, each pass's half period 2 E + the patched step
$9628 SoundSweepNow
