$96D1 ShiftBC1
@module scanner ; The scanner, the condition light, the energy and the shields, the missile
@about The scanner is the ellipse in the middle of the dashboard. Its background (13 bytes by 48 lines from $5049) is kept in ScannerSave $5B00 and copied back each frame before the ships are drawn (ScannerRestore). A ship within range ($40 in the high byte of each coordinate and x² + z² below $1600 in squares' units) is a dot of two or three pixels at (x * 3/16, z * 5/64) from the centre $558F, with a stalk of y * 5/64 lines up or down to it.
@about The per-frame dashboard work (DashboardTick) prints the indicators, handles the missile keys and the damage, and recharges the energy banks. Condition $7104 is worked out again every frame: green by default, yellow while a ship other than the station is about (ConditionYellow), red with a shield down, flashing ($63) with the fourth energy bank not full; ConditionLight puts it on the two cells of the light and sets green for the next frame.

$96D6 c ScannerNext ; The next slot
$96D9 c DrawScanner ; Restore the scanner's background, then a dot and a stalk for each ship within range
> Nothing is drawn while no slot is in use (ShipsPresent $9C96); a free slot has energy (+$22) 0; 553 of 1076 calls drew in f1, w1 and d1. The coordinates go through Divide16 with DE = $4000, so a high byte of $40 would be the scanner's edge.
$96ED ScannerShip
$9725 ScannerPlace
$9745 DrawScannerSetSoundBit1
$9765 DrawScannerSetSoundBit2
$9785 DrawScannerSetSoundBit3
$9788 ScannerScreen ; HL = the centre; x moves it by bytes and C gets the pixel
