@module shipmotion ; The escape pod, the vectors, the ship loop and the motion: rotation, movement, tidying
@about A ship slot is 39 bytes (ShipSlots $6048, slot 0 the station, slots 1-6 the other ships, slot 7 the player's missile and the title's ship). +$00, +$03, +$06: x, y, z, each three bytes (low, high, then the top bits with the sign in bit 7). +$09, +$0F, +$15: the three axes (nose, roof, side), three words each whose high byte is sign and magnitude, $7FFF one. +$1B speed, +$1C acceleration, +$1D and +$1E the roll and pitch counters (bits 0-3 the steps, bit 6 the direction, bit 7 for ever), +$20 the flags (bits 0-2 the ships it may launch, bit 3 fired, bits 4-5 the explosion, bit 6 tactics on, bit 7 an escape pod), +$21 the behaviour (bit 2 hostile, bits 5-6 protected), +$22 the energy (0 a free slot), +$23 the blueprint, +$25 the tactics state, +$26 the role (bit 0 a missile, 1 scoopable, 2 the station, 3 passive). The layout matches zx-elite's DATA-STRUCTURES; each field here is the one this code reads.
@about The player never moves: every frame each ship is rotated about the origin by the player's roll and pitch and moved along z by the player's speed (MovePosition), then turned by its own counters (TurnShip) and moved along its own nose by its own speed (MoveShip). The axes drift from unit length and right angles and are tidied every frame (TidyAxis).

$9C1C c EscapePod ; Q with an escape pod, not in witch space (WitchSpace): the pod is launched and the cargo, the pod and the legal status lost
> Clears the cargo hold ($D06B, 17 bytes) and the fugitive bit of $D0B0, empties the hold to 20 tons free, 35 with the large cargo bay (FreeSpace $D07C), launches ship $17 (the pod as the player's ship) and counts 24 frames down to the arrival at the station (Arrived $71BA). m1 launched it at frame 2534 (Q), and m2 before its dock.
$9C29 EscapePodKey
$9C50 EscapePodCargo
$9C68 EscapePodHold
