$9EF1 c SquareRoot ; HL = the square root of HL, scaled up or down to keep 12 bits of precision
> Below $1000 the value is shifted up by 8 (or 4) and the root down by 4 (or 2). Two steps of Newton's iteration (SquareRootCore).
$9EFB SquareRootLoop
$9F0A SquareRootSmall
$9F11 SquareRootShift
$9F18 c SquareRootCore ; Two Newton steps from $8000: r = (r + n / r) / 2
$9F2B c SquareRootStep
$9F35 c SquareRootAdd
$9F41 c TidyAxis ; Bring an axis back to unit length: each part times 1 - (x² + y² + z² - 1) / 2 from the high bytes
> The correction is the sum of the three high bytes' squares (the table $BF00, index 2 x) / 4, negated with the sign in bit 7; TidyPart multiplies each high byte by it. 4650 runs: the three axes of each ship drawn.
$9F68 c TidyPart ; One part times the correction (B), keeping its sign
