@module tactics ; The title's ship and the ships' tactics: energy, launches, fleeing, the missile's homing, steering and firing
@about Tactics run for a ship with bit 6 of its flags set, every fourth frame per slot (UpdateSlotAlive); a missile homes every frame. Each pass the ship regains energy, may launch a ship of its own (a trader's escape pod, the station's traffic or a Thargoid's Thargons), may flee or bail out when weak, then steers: TacticsSteer takes the unit vector to its target (the player at the origin, or away from the player), its dot products with the ship's three axes give the roll, the pitch and the acceleration, and a hostile ship facing the player close enough fires its laser.
@about Random $B799 gives the numbers: a 16-bit additive generator at RandomSeed $B7AA.

$A28B b RateSpare 2 ; Two zero bytes no code reads (known from the code only)
$A28D c TurnTitleShip ; Turn the title's ship (slot 7) by fixed rates, tidy its roof and side axes and draw it
> Roll $94 (TurnRates) and pitch $8C (A) through MoveShip with the ship's own speed; 393 runs (the title of f1, w1, d1).
$A2B8 b TargetVector 2 ; The vector to the target (three words), its length after Normalise ($A2BE)
$A2C0 c Tactics ; Energy, launches, fleeing or bailing out, the station's traffic, then steering
> Energy: one more a pass (four more above $F0 of the blueprint's maximum, +$07), up to it. A weak ship (energy x 2 below the maximum): with launches left (+$20 bits 0-2) and the random byte below $80 and no ECM it launches its payload: ship action 4 of the kind in the blueprint's +$0A high nibble (a Thargoid's Thargons, the station's ships), or a missile at the player (action 2) when the nibble is 0, a trader with a pod may bail out (action 7: the pod, then the ship becomes passive cargo), or cargo is dropped (action 6). The cloak ship (MissionShip $9CB2): 1 (cloaked) becomes 2 (seen) below $34 energy, 2 goes back to 1 at $50 and more. While the player is cloaked (CloakOn $D041) no ship runs its tactics. The station (role bit 2) launches a ship at random when fewer than 4 are active: a Viper ($14 hostile, the station angry) or traffic ($24 / $44).
