@module drawships ; Drawing a ship: the view's axes, the dot of a far ship, the vertices projected, the visible edges, the laser beams
@about A ship is drawn in the back buffer only in the four space views (ViewIndex 0-3). The view picks the depth axis: z for the front and rear views, x for the side views (bit 1), and the sign that is "ahead" (bit 0); a ship behind the view or past 256 in depth is not drawn. Its screen position is depth-divided (DividePoint $AC69: x / depth and y / depth as fractions) and must lie within 128 x 64 of the centre. Beyond the blueprint's dot distance (+$0B) it is four pixels; nearer, the full wireframe: the visible faces (FaceVisibility $BCD4) and the vertices whose faces are visible are rotated into the view (Project), their screen points kept in ProjectedPoints $A8FA, then each edge with a visible face is drawn (DrawEdges). The detail level is the distance too: a vertex or an edge whose visibility distance (the low 5 bits, $1F always) is below the ship's distance is skipped.
@about The arithmetic is quarter squares: b x c = ((b + c) / 2)² - ((b - c) / 2)² from the squares table (n² for n = 0-255, the low bytes at $BE00 and the high at $BF00, built by the kickoff), so Multiply8 $AB34 is two table reads and a subtraction.

$A6DF c DrawShip ; Draw one ship in the view: the depth, the screen position, the gunsight test, then the dot or the wireframe
> 1681 runs. The ship in the gunsight is the one whose screen point is within its own size of the centre with depth below $2C00 (SightTarget $9C97); a hostile ship with tactics that nears the player ahead turns off its avoidance (+$26 bit 5). A destroyed ship (+$20 bit 4) is not drawn: its screen point and size go into +$1C-+$1F for the explosion (ExplosionPoint). The mission's Asp is not drawn while the mission state is 1.
$A6F1 DrawShipDepth
$A70F DrawShipNear
