@module combat ; Collisions and scooping, the player's laser and the gunsight, the ECM, the ship actions and spawning, face visibility
@about ShipAction $B867 does every creation: A's low nibble is the action and the high nibble its argument C. 0 a new ship in the system (SpawnShip), 1 a group of Thargoids, 2 a missile (C = 0: from the ship at IX at the player; else the player's at slot C's ship), 3 nothing, 4 a ship launched from IX (C picks the kind), 5 alloy plates, 6 a cargo canister, 7 an escape pod (C = 1: the player's own Cobra flying off), 8 two splinters, 9 the title's ship C + 2 in slot 7. A new ship (CreateShip) is the 31-byte template ShipTemplate plus its blueprint's energy, behaviour, payload, half its top speed, the tactics state $7E and a random position near $3200 on each axis unless it is hostile.

$B4D7 b LaserFired ; The laser fired last frame (LaserCooling); B4D6 the beam's random bits
$B4D6 b LaserBeam
$B4D8 c Collide ; A ship inside the player's box: scooped, docked, or both hit
> The box is the blueprint's size (+$01; 180 for scoopables; z one more page for a missile with no target) on each axis, with z ahead only. Scoopable and below (y negative) with the fuel scoop ($D088): the slot is freed and the hold gains one of the cargo in the blueprint's +$00 high nibble (or a random 0-7, or the mission's item) through AddCargo $D0E4, if the hold has room ($D07C). The station: ahead, upright (its nose's z negative, the roof's within $3C) and not hostile docks (Docked = 1); else a crash costs the front shield $0C + 2 x speed. Anything else is destroyed and its size hits the front or aft shield. The sun or the planet too near (TooClose) skips this. dk docked at frame 2190, cs scooped a plate at 910 (AddCargo); a crash is known from the code only.
$B4F0 CollideScoopable
$B4F8 CollideBox
$B51A CollideInside
$B53A CollideScoopCargo
$B548 CollideScoopMission
$B555 CollideScoopRandom
$B55A CollideScoopAdd
$B55D CollideStation
$B595 CollideStationCrash
$B5A8 CollideShip
$B5BF CollideShipSound
$B5D3 CollideTooHard
$B5D8 CollideShipFront
$B5DF c RemoveShip ; A ship gone: every missile aimed at it explodes, and the player's missile loses its lock on it
$B5EE RemoveShipLoop
$B600 RemoveShipNext
$B618 c ShipsWreck ; The player's death: the explosion's sound, the front view, every slot free, then a canister and two plates near (actions $16 and $15)
$B62A ShipsWreckLoop
$B63C c LaserCooling ; The laser temperature falls by 2 a frame; A (the fire key, KeyCombat bit 0) fires the view's laser below $90
> LaserMounts $D07D (one byte per view): 1 pulse, 2 beam, 3 military, 4 mining (EquipLaser). A press fires at once; held, a pulse laser fires every other pass and a mining one every eighth (JumpEncounter's low bits, D = 1 or 7), a beam or military laser every pass. Each shot is drain 1, the laser sound and heat $08 (pulse, mining) or $0A (beam, military), capped at $A0. The power is $0F (pulse, beam), $17 (military), $32 (mining). A hit on SightTarget turns it hostile, its tactics state down by 14, and its energy down by the power; at 0 it is destroyed ($FF), and gives a canister of alloys (action 6), an asteroid splinters (5), the mining laser on a Rock Hermit or a boulder plates (8), or ends the mission ship (3). 30 recorded frames fired; none hit.
$B64D LaserCool
$B672 LaserKind
$B678 LaserRate
$B686 LaserShot
