@module squaretable ; The table of squares and the back buffer
@about The kickoff builds the table of squares (n² for n = 0-255: the low bytes at $BE00, the high bytes at $BF00) where the tape carries zeros, and copies $C800-$CFFF over the Lenslok's code at $C000 (03-build-and-load.md 3.7). The game then uses $C000-$CFFF as the back buffer of the 3D view: the top two thirds of a screen in the screen's own layout, drawn there, copied to $4000 each frame. The bytes here are the image as the kickoff leaves it: the back buffer still holds what the loader put there.

$BE00 b SquaresLow 16 ; n² AND $FF for n = 0-255 (Square, Multiply8, VectorLength, SquareRoot)
> c1 reads the table back as n² for every n at frame 18018; f1, w1 and d1 read it in every multiplication.
$BF00 b SquaresHigh 16 ; n² / 256 for n = 0-255
$C000 b BackBuffer 32 ; The 3D view's back buffer ($C000-$CFFF, the layout of $4000-$4FFF): ClearView clears it, the lines and the circles draw into it, CopyBackBuffer copies it to the screen; docked, its last bytes are the screens' stack (CallScreen sets SP to $D000)
@module gamestate ; The screen table and the vectors, the commander record, the dashboard messages, the full-page messages, cash, legal status and cargo
@about The top part of the game is reached through the vectors at $D000-$D0F5: ScreenTable for the docked screens and the charts (CallScreen patches its CALL to $D000 + 3 x the screen), then the printer, the jump keys and the commander menu. The commander record $D054-$D0B9 (102 bytes, the block the tape saves and loads) is a copy of the default commander DefaultCommander $D232 after a new game; before that, at load time, its bytes are the kickoff code that started the game (docs/03-build-and-load.md 3.7). The fields: the name (10 letters), the legal status ($D05F), the combat score ($D060, three bytes), the galaxy, the cash, the cargo hold ($D06B, 17 commodities), the free space ($D07C), the lasers ($D07D, four views), the fuel ($D082), the missiles ($D083), the equipment flags ($D084-$D08D), the galaxy's and the system's seeds, the market's stock ($D09E), the mission state ($D0AF) and flags ($D0B0). The layout agrees with zx-elite's COMMANDER-STATE and DATA-STRUCTURES; the addresses here are this image's.
@about The dashboard messages are ten slots at $D0BD (a byte with bit 7 the request, then an argument): the code sets a bit and ShowMessage prints it in the message line over a few frames.

$D000 c ScreenBuy ; ScreenTable 0: buy cargo (the key 2 docked)
$D003 c ScreenSell ; ScreenTable 1: sell cargo (3)
$D006 c ScreenEquip ; ScreenTable 2: equip the ship (4)
$D009 c ScreenGalaxy ; ScreenTable 3: the galactic chart (I)
$D00C c ScreenLocal ; ScreenTable 4: the local chart (O)
$D00F c ScreenData ; ScreenTable 5: the data on a system (P)
$D012 c ScreenMarket ; ScreenTable 6: the market prices (K)
$D015 c ScreenStatus ; ScreenTable 7: the commander's status (L), also after a dock
$D018 c ScreenInventory ; ScreenTable 8: the inventory (ENTER)
$D01B c CursorLeft ; ScreenTable 9-15: the chart keys (ChartCursorKeys): 9 left (N, KeySteer bit 0), the cursor one x less (ChartLeft)
$D01E c CursorRight ; 10: right (M), ChartRight
$D021 c CursorDown ; 11: down (X), two y more, ChartDown
$D024 c CursorUp ; 12: up (S), ChartUp
$D027 c CursorHome ; 13: B (KeyChart bit 4), the cursor back on the current system (ChartHome)
$D02A c CursorDistance ; 14: D (KeyChart bit 5), the nearest system's name and distance (ShowSelected)
$D02D c PlanetNameVector ; 15: R (KeyChart bit 6), PLANET NAME? (PlanetNamePrompt)
$D030 c NextGalaxyVector ; ScreenTable 16: NextGalaxy: no key and no caller asks for 16 (CallScreen gets 0-15), so it is never reached
$D033 c NewGameVector ; NewGame $D298
$D036 c ClearScreenVector ; ClearScreen $D61D: the page cleared, its frame drawn
$D039 c PrintOtherVector ; PrintOther $D45F: the other token set
$D03C c ViewTextsVector ; ViewTexts $DA7A: the view's texts and the countdown
$D03F b TunnelOn ; A launch or dock tunnel is running
$D040 b TunnelLoop ; The tunnel's frames run inside one call; the views are locked meanwhile
$D041 b CloakOn ; Non-zero while the cloaking device is on (CloakKey): the view tinted blue, the energy drain one more; ENERGY LOW turns it off
$D042 c JumpKeysVector ; JumpKeys $DBA2: the hyperspace keys (in the interrupt)
$D045 b TextColumn ; The print position: the column and the row
$D046 b TextRow
$D047 b MissileState ; 0 off, 1 armed, 2 locked
$D048 c PrintCodeVector ; PrintCode $D425: the standard token set
$D04B w PrintTarget ; The address of the printer's plot byte ($D548): $A9 (XOR C) mixes a glyph into the screen, $00 (NOP) writes it over (the dashboard's indicators)
$D04D b PrintSpare
$D04E c CommanderMenuVector ; CommanderMenu $D90A: load or save a commander
$D051 b CrossX ; The chart's crosshair: x, y and the circle's radius
$D052 b CrossY
$D053 b ChartRadius
$D054 t CommanderName ; The commander record: the name, 10 letters and a zero
$D05F b LegalStatus ; 0 clean, up to 49 an offender, 50 or more a fugitive; bit 6 set by a protected kill
$D060 b CombatScore 3 ; The combat score (the rating): the low byte, then two
$D063 b CommanderRest 8 ; The jumps, the galaxy, the cash and the price fluctuation
$D06B b CargoHold 17 ; The tons (or kg, g) of each commodity
$D07C b FreeSpace ; The hold's free space in tons
$D07D b LaserMounts 4 ; The laser of each view: 0 none, 1 pulse, 2 beam, 3 military, 4 mining
$D081 b NovaMission ; The record's +$2D: 1 in the system whose sun goes nova (JumpArrive after 32 jumps), until the jump out; the red tint, the refugees' question (RefugeeQuestion)
$D082 b Fuel ; The fuel in tenths of a light year
$D083 b Missiles ; The missiles fitted (0-4)
$D084 b Equipment 10 ; The equipment flags: the large cargo bay, ECM, two spare, the fuel scoop, the escape pod, the energy bomb, the energy unit, the docking computer, the galactic hyperdrive
$D08E b Seeds 16 ; The spare bytes, the galaxy's three seeds, the system's three seeds
$D09E b MarketStock 17 ; The station's stock of each commodity
$D0AF b MissionState ; The Thargoid mission: 0 none, 1 the MAYDAY heard, 2 not yet answered, 3 accepted, 4 in the galaxy's first system (the station a Thargoid base), $0C its station destroyed, 5 rewarded at the next dock
$D0B0 b MissionFlags ; Bit 0 the nova started (32 jumps), 1 the cloak ship due (128 jumps), 2 the Thargoid MAYDAY started (254 jumps), 3 the Thargoid mission done, 5 refugees aboard, 6 the cloaking device owned, 7 the Thargoid mission accepted (the ECM jammer)
$D0B1 b RecordTail 9 ; The record's last nine bytes: the system docked at ($D0B2, $D0B3) and the sun's place
$D0BA b SunGrows ; Past the record: the sun's growth
$D0BB b ChartCursorX ; The chart cursor (galaxy coordinates)
$D0BC b ChartCursorY
$D0BD b Messages 2 ; Ten message slots (MessageTick): a column (bit 7 the request) and a standard code each
> 0 MISSILE JAMMED, 1 INCOMING MISSILE, 2 TARGET LOST, 3 an item DESTROYED (DamageItem), 4 a bounty in CR (AddCash), 5 a scooped item's name (AddCargo writes the code), 6 RIGHT ON COMMANDER (a new rating), 9 FUEL LEAK (FuelLeak); slots 7 and 8 ($D0CB-$D0CE) are the number printer's work bytes and never requested.
$D0D1 b PrintCase ; The printer's case state: the mode, the capital-next flags, the word buffering
$D0D2 b PrintCapital
$D0D3 b PrintCapitalNext
$D0D4 b PrintBuffering
