$D0DA c ClearHighlightsVector
$D0DD c MissionQuestionVector
$D0E0 c TradeDoneVector
$D0E3 b MissileTarget ; The slot the missile is locked on
$D0E4 c AddCargoVector ; AddCargo $D190: a scooped item
$D0E7 c AddCashVector ; AddCash $D1D9: a bounty
$D0EA c AddCombatVector ; AddCombat $D1C7: the combat score
$D0ED c MissionDoneVector ; MissionDone $D14D
$D0F0 b VectorSpare
$D0F3 c DamageVector ; DamageItem $D1E9: a hit that went through the shields
$D0F6 c FullMessage ; A game over page: SHIP BOARDED BY (other $0B), other token A ($0D PIRATE, $D4 THARGON) and S, THEY SHOW NO MERCY... (other $FF), a click, a key, the page cleared
$D114 FullMessageWait
$D123 c MissionQuestion ; WANTED BY GALCOP: A BRAVE COMMANDER FOR A SPECIAL MISSION, ARE YOU INTERESTED (Y/N)? (other $DF); Y: state 3, flag bit 7 and the briefing (other $E0); any other key: state 0
$D138 MissionAccept
$D148 MissionText
$D14D c MissionDone ; The Thargoid mission's award: the combat score's high byte one more, state 0, flag bit 3, IN APPRECIATION OF YOUR EXCEPTIONAL COURAGE ... (other $0A)
$D162 c ColourPage ; Clear the page, other token $5C (a capital next), all 768 attributes E, the position HL, then other token D
$D177 ColourPageFill
$D183 c AddCargoSpecial ; $FF: the cloak ship's canister: the cloaking device (flag bit 6), the combat score's high byte one more, CLOAKING DEVICE on the message line
$D190 c AddCargo ; One unit of commodity A into the hold (one less free space), the message, and the legal cost of the contraband
> Firearms ($0A) cost 2, slaves (3) and narcotics (6) cost 4 on LegalStatus, up to $FF.
$D1A3 AddCargoMessage
$D1AD AddCargoContraband ; The legal cost of commodity A (BuyCheck enters here for each unit bought)
$D1B8 AddCargoLegal4
$D1BA AddCargoLegal
$D1C5 AddCargoStore
$D1C7 c AddCombat ; The combat score plus DE; a carry into the third byte flags the rating message ($D0C9)
$D1D9 c AddCash ; The cash plus DE (a bounty) and the message ($D0C5)
$D1E6 AddCashMessage
$D1E9 c DamageItem ; A random loss: below 1 the fuel, 1-6 a piece of equipment, 7-16 a unit of cargo (StarSeed's bits)
> 25 runs in f1 and w1 (the ships' lasers), none lost anything: every random pick was empty or 17 and above.
$D209 DamageItemEquip
$D20F DamageItemLost
$D213 DamageItemMessage
$D21F DamageItemCargo
$D232 b DefaultCommander 8 ; The new game's commander: JAMESON, 100.0 Cr, 7.0 light years of fuel, a pulse laser, 3 missiles, galaxy 1 at Lave
$D28F b DefaultSun 9 ; The new game's sun and planet place
$D298 c NewGame ; The default commander copied in, the chart cursor on Lave, the prices made (MakeMarket with its stock store patched to a NOP: the stock is the record's), the sun placed
@module textprint ; Numbers, cash, the two token sets, the character printer, rules and bars, the random synonyms
@about Two interpreters print the game's texts (tools/tokens.py decodes both). PrintCode $D425, the standard set: below $0E a control code (TokenControl), $0E-$1F tokens $80-$91, $20-$5F characters, $60-$7F tokens 0-$1F, $80-$9F two-letter pairs ($FDB3), $A0 and up tokens 0-$5F; token n is the n-th zero-ended string of the table at TokenTable ($F11A). PrintOther $D45F, the other set (the table at $F11C): string n-1 for token n, its codes below $20 controls (OtherControl), up to $5A characters, $5B-$80 a random pick of one of five tokens (RandomToken, the synonym rows at $D5F5), $81-$D6 other tokens, $D7 and up pairs ($FD99). Both print through PrintChar, which keeps the case (capitals at a word's start, the rest small, by PrintCase) and either plots or buffers the letter for the justified text.
@about A letter is plotted from the font at $5D70 into the screen at (TextColumn, TextRow) with XOR (or over, by the byte at $D548); the column wraps at 32.
@inline $D421 1 ; PrintInline: the code byte after the CALL
@inline $E2BC 1 ; ColumnInline: the column byte after the CALL

$D2DC w NumberLeft ; The number being printed, less the digits printed so far
