@module chartcursor ; The charts' crosses: the cursor's cross placed and drawn with XOR, the cursor keys' moves
@about A chart cross is two XOR lines through (CrossX, CrossY), CrossSize long, clipped to the chart (CrossTop to CrossBottom, and the screen's sides): drawing it twice takes it away, so every cursor move is erase, move, draw. The galactic chart's cursor cross is 10 pixels and sits at the cursor's chart point (x, y / 2 + 24); the short range chart's is 16, at 4 pixels a unit of x and 2 of y from the current system at the chart's centre (97, 96), and is not drawn off the chart.

$E46F c ChartCross ; The cursor's cross on the chart that is up, by CrossSize: 10 the galactic chart, else the short range one (nothing when off it)
> 36 runs (f1, d1: the charts and their cursor). The short range point: x = 97 + 4 (cursor x - current x), y = 96 + 2 (cursor y - current y), refused on any overflow and outside rows 25-166.
