@module market ; Buying and selling cargo and equipment: the quantity editor, the checks and the undo, the nova's refugees
@about The three docked trading screens (keys 2, 3 and 4) walk the 17 commodities or the 14 equipment items with the pointers of MarketRow / HoldRow. For each row the player types a quantity (QuantityKeys: one or two digits, ENTER skips the row, another key leaves the page); every digit runs the screen's check (BuyCheck, SellCheck, EquipAccept) on a copy of the cash, the hold, the stock and the free space (SaveTrade), and a refusal (QUANTITY?, CASH?, CARGO?) puts the copy back (RestoreTrade). No recording traded: the module is known from the code only, except the pages' headings (d1).
@about The nova mission's two pages live here too: docking in the nova's system asks THE SUN IS GOING NOVA, WILL YOU SAVE US (Y/N)?; Y fits a large cargo bay and fills the hold with refugees (MissionFlags bit 5); docking anywhere else with them aboard gives 100 units of gem-stones and the bay (35 tons) back.

