@module dockedscreens ; The docked screens of ScreenTable: the galactic and the short range charts, the data on a system, the market prices, the status and the inventory
@about The six letter keys draw these pages (SelectView through CallScreen): I the galactic chart, O the short range chart, P the data on the selected system, K the market prices, L the commander's status, ENTER the inventory. Each page is text through PrintCode / PrintOther with the colour bands of ColourBands; the two charts plot instead: the galactic chart a dot for each of the 256 systems (through the ROM's PIXEL-ADD $22AA and a SET patched to the dot's bit), the short range chart an icon for each system within 19 x and 34 y of the current one and its name on a free text row.
@about Witnesses: the galactic chart 1 run, the short range chart 3, the data screen 1 (the data on Lave), the market prices 1, the status 3 (d1); the inventory 3 runs in t1, 1 in dk, 2 in m1.
@inline $F068 1 ; PrintIfFitted: the code byte after the CALL

$EB7C c GalacticChart ; Screen I: the 256 systems as dots, the current system's cross (16) and its fuel circle, the cursor's cross (10), GALACTIC CHART
> The chart is the galaxy at half height: a system's dot is at (x, y / 2 + 24), x = s1 high, y = s0 high, so rows 24-151 hold it (CrossTop 24, CrossBottom 152). The fuel circle's radius is the fuel / 4 (7.0 light years = 70 tenths: 17 pixels). The text rows 0-2 and 19-23 are cleared (ClearBlock), the bottom five rows coloured $17 under a rule at $5060 for the cursor's name and distance. 1 run.
$EBE3 GalacticChartLoop
$EBEE c ClearBlock ; A x 32 bytes before HL cleared on each of the cell's eight pixel rows: SP at HL and PUSHes of zero, the interrupts off
> HL = $4060, A = 3 clears the character rows 0-2; HL = $5100, A = 5 the rows 19-23. PUSH writes below SP, so HL is the block's end. 2 runs.
$EBFB ClearBlockRow
$EBFF ClearBlockCells
$EC01 ClearBlockPush
$EC11 b ClearBlockCount ; ClearBlock's A (the rows of 32 bytes)
$EC12 w ClearBlockStack ; ClearBlock's saved SP
$EC14 c PlotSystem ; The dot of the system in SystemSeeds at (x, y / 2 + 24): PIXEL-ADD $22AA, its bit patched into the SET at $EC35
> PIXEL-ADD counts y from the bottom, so B = (y / 2 XOR 127) + 24 is 175 less the row. It returns the bit's place in the byte in A (0 the left); XOR 7, times 8, OR $C0 is the second byte of SET n,B, written into the instruction. 256 runs.
$EC3B c ClampLow ; A = 0: the window's low edge when cx - 19 or cy - 34 went below 0
$EC3D c ClampHigh ; A = 255: its high edge when cx + 19 or cy + 34 passed 255
$EC40 b RowsUsed 24 ; The short range chart's text rows that hold a name (255), one byte a row
$EC58 c ShortRangeChart ; Screen O: SHORT RANGE CHART, the systems near the current one as icons with their names, the current system's cross (24), the fuel circle, the cursor's cross (16)
> The window is the current system's x ± 19 and y ± 34, written into the four CP operands of EachSystemInWindow ($ECDF, $ECE3, $ECEA, $ECEE). A system is 4 pixels a unit of x and 2 of y from the centre (97, 96); the fuel circle's radius is the fuel (70 pixels for 7.0 light years). Two walks: the icons (DrawSystemIcon) then the names (LabelSystem), so a name never lands under an icon drawn after it. 3 runs.
$EC5E ShortRangeChartClear
$ECD2 c EachSystemInWindow ; The 256 systems: those inside the window (x and y each low <= v < high) handed to the routine at HL (the CALL at $ECF1 patched)
> 6 runs (two a chart), 60 systems handed on: 10 a chart around Lave.
$ECDA EachSystemLoop
$ECF1 EachSystemCall ; CALL patched to DrawSystemIcon or LabelSystem (they step to the next system themselves)
$ECF6 EachSystemSkip
$ECF9 EachSystemNext
$ECFD c SystemPixel ; HL = the screen address of the system's icon (its top left at x 94 + 4 dx, row 93 + 2 dy from the current system), A its bit, B and C the coordinates
> dx and dy are the system's x and y less the current system's; the icon is 8 x 8, so its centre is the cross's (97, 96) for dx = dy = 0. 60 runs.
$ED27 c DrawSystemIcon ; One of the four ChartIcons (s2 high AND $18: 8 bytes each) XORed in at the system's place, shifted A bits across two bytes, then the next system
> The shift A is written into the LD B at $ED47. The icon's eight rows step down the screen's thirds as NextRowDown does. 30 runs.
$ED3A DrawSystemIconRows
$ED3C DrawSystemIconRow
$ED48 DrawSystemIconShift
$ED4E DrawSystemIconXor
$ED6D DrawSystemIconDown
$ED6E DrawSystemIconNext
$ED75 b LabelSpare 2 ; Two bytes no code reads (known from the code only)
$ED77 b LabelLength ; LabelSystem writes 8 - the name's length here, and no code reads it (known from the code only)
$ED78 c LabelSystem ; The system's name at the text cell right of its icon: its own row, else the row above (from row 3), else the row below (to row 22), else none
> The column is the icon's x / 8 + 1, the row 22 less the icon's B / 8 rounded up. 30 runs: the ten names around Lave (Diso, Leesti, Orrere, Reorte, Riedquat, Uszaa, Zaonce, Tionisla, Orerve and Lave itself) on each of three charts.
$EDA4 LabelSystemRow
$EDBC LabelSystemBelow
$EDC5 c PrintIfRowFree ; The name in NameBuffer at TextRow unless RowsUsed has it: the row marked and the name printed (carry), else no carry
> 39 runs for 30 names: nine names took a second row.
$EDDF c DataScreen ; Screen P: DATA ON <system> for the system nearest the cursor: the distance, the economy, government, tech level, population and species, productivity, radius, and its description
> The species is in brackets after the population; the productivity has " M CR", the radius " km" (PrintUnit with MarketItem 17). The description is other token 5 (TextRandom from TextSeeds = s1, s2), or IS RESISTING A THARGON INVASION (other $DE) for the galaxy's first system while a Thargoid mission is on (MissionState not 0). 1 run (d1, the data on Lave: Rich Agricultural, Dictatorship, Tech.Level 5, Population 2.5 Billion (Human Colonials), Gross Productivity 7000 M CR, Average Radius 4116 km).
$EE8C DataScreenDescription
$EE9D c PrintCodeGap ; Standard code A, a new line and an empty line
$EEA2 c NewLineGap ; A new line and an empty line
$EEA5 NewLineGapSecond
$EEA8 c PrintEconomy ; ECONOMY: and RICH / AVERAGE / POOR / MAINLY (codes $AA-$AD) and INDUSTRIAL or AGRICULTURAL (economy / 4: codes $A8, $A9)
> Economy 0-3 take $AA + e, 5-7 $AA + e - 5, 4 MAINLY: 0 rich, 1 average, 2 poor, 3 mainly industrial, 4 mainly, 5 rich, 6 average, 7 poor agricultural, as the BBC's.
$EEB8 PrintEconomyKind
$EEBD PrintEconomyType
$EEC8 PrintEconomyMainly
$EECE c PrintSpecies ; The system's people: HUMAN COLONIALS (s2 low below $80), else up to three adjectives and the kind, as the BBC's
> s2 high bits 2-4 below 3: LARGE, FIERCE, SMALL (codes $E3-$E5); bits 5-7 below 6: GREEN, RED, YELLOW, BLUE, BLACK, HARMLESS ($E6-$EB); (s0 high XOR s1 high) AND 7 below 6: SLIMY, BUG-EYED, HORNED, BONY, FAT, FURRY ($EC-$F1); the kind ((that + s2 high AND 3) AND 7): RODENTS to INSECTS ($F2-$F9). Lave's people: s2 low below $80.
$EEDA PrintSpeciesAlien
$EEEB PrintSpeciesColour
$EEFB PrintSpeciesLook
$EF11 PrintSpeciesKind
$EF1E PrintSpeciesEnd
$EF21 c PrintRadius ; The radius in km: ((s2 high AND 15) + 11) x 256 + s1 high, five digits
$EF37 c IsFirstSystem ; No carry when the selected system is the galaxy's first (its six seeds the galaxy's)
> m2 ran it once, from JumpTick through MissionTriggers at frame 5183: the jump to Ausis, galaxy 2's first system, made MissionState 3 into 4 (the Thargoid base).
$EF3C IsFirstSystemLoop
$EF46 IsFirstSystemNo
$EF48 c MarketPrices ; Screen K: <system> MARKET PRICES, the heading line (code $FF) and the 17 commodities (MarketRow); in witch space only the heading
> 1 run (the Lave market of d1).
$EF79 MarketPricesLoop
$EF86 b StatusLaserView ; The view the status page's laser line is at (0-3)
$EF87 c StatusScreen ; Screen L: COMMANDER <name>, the present and the hyperspace systems, the fuel, the cash, the legal status, the rating, the equipment and the lasers
> The legal status: CLEAN (0), OFFENDER (1-49), FUGITIVE (50 and more). The rating: while the combat score's top byte is 0 its middle byte against 8, 16, 32, 64, 128 (HARMLESS, MOSTLY HARMLESS, POOR, AVERAGE, ABOVE AVERAGE: the first threshold at or above it, COMPETENT past 128), else the top byte against 2, 10, 25 (COMPETENT, DANGEROUS, DEADLY), ELITE past 25 (RatingScores). The equipment lines: LARGE CARGO BAY, FUEL SCOOPS, the E.C.M. SYSTEM JAMMER (MissionFlags bit 7) or E.C.M. SYSTEM, ENERGY BOMB, ENERGY UNIT, DOCKING COMPUTERS, GALACTIC HYPERSPACE, the four lasers (FRONT PULSE LASER...), CLOAKING DEVICE (bit 6). The escape pod ($D089) has no line. 3 runs.
$EFD2 StatusOffender
$EFD3 StatusLegal
$EFEF StatusRatingHigh
$EFF4 StatusRatingLoop
$EFFC StatusRating
$F026 StatusEcm
$F02D StatusBomb
$F053 StatusLasersLoop
$F065 StatusFrame
$F068 c PrintIfFitted ; A not 0: the code byte after the CALL on its own line at column 5; the return past the byte either way
> 21 runs: seven equipment lines a status page.
$F072 c EquipmentLine ; A new line, column 5
$F07A c PrintLaser ; The laser of the next view (StatusLaserView one more): FRONT / REAR / LEFT / RIGHT and PULSE / BEAM / MILITARY / MINING LASER; nothing for none
> Codes $60 + view, then $66 + kind for 1-2 (PULSE LASER $67, BEAM LASER $68), $72 + kind for 3-4 (MILITARY $75, MINING $76). 12 runs: four a page.
$F098 PrintLaserPulse
$F09A PrintLaserName
$F0A1 c StatusSystem ; Column 21, ":" and standard control A (2 the current system, 3 the selected one), a new line
$F0AE b RatingScores 6 ; The rating's thresholds for the score's middle byte (8, 16, 32, 64, 128, end $FF)
$F0B4 b RatingHigh 4 ; Those for its top byte (2, 10, 25, end $FF)
$F0B8 c InventoryScreen ; Screen ENTER: INVENTORY, the fuel, the cash, LARGE CARGO BAY (its line coloured), REFUGEES (MissionFlags bit 5), the hold (HoldRow for each commodity)
> t1 (3 runs from frame 848), dk and m1 showed it.
$F0EB InventoryRefugees
$F0FD InventoryHold
$F107 InventoryHoldLoop
@module keyboard ; The text tables, the key bytes, the keyboard scan, the joysticks, the steering accumulators and the IM2 interrupt
@about Every frame the IM2 interrupt (IM2Handler, through the vector $FEFE that I = $FD and a floating bus byte $FF give) scans the eight keyboard half-rows (ScanKeyboard): each key down sets its bit in one of the key bytes $FC08-$FC0C or KeyDigits (KeyTable: an offset and a mask a key) and leaves its character in KeyCode. Then the joystick (Options bits 0-1: keyboard, Kempston, Cursor, Sinclair) replaces the four steering bits, Options bits 4 and 5 reverse both axes or the vertical one, and ReadControls turns the steering bits into the roll, pitch and speed accumulators the flight loop copies (CopyRates). The game code reads and clears the key bytes; nothing else polls the keyboard.
@about The key bytes: KeyScreens $FC08 (ENTER, L, K, P, O, I, 0, Y), KeySteer $FC09 (N, M, X, S, SPACE, SYMBOL SHIFT), KeyViews $FC0A (1-4, H, G, J, CAPS SHIFT), KeyCombat $FC0B (A, T, F, U, E, W, Q, C), KeyChart $FC0C (B, D, R) and KeyDigits $FC0F (9, 5, 8, 6, 7). Z and V set no bit. All three recordings steered with the keyboard (Options $8C: sound, recentring and damping on): the joysticks are known from the code only.

$F117 b TextSpare 3 ; Three bytes no code reads (known from the code only)
$F11A w TokenTable ; The standard tokens' address ($F11E): PrintCode skips n zero-ended strings from it
$F11C w OtherTable ; The other tokens' address ($F4F5): PrintOther skips n - 1
$F11E b StdTokens ; The standard set's 149 strings (tools/tokens.py --set std), each ended by a zero
@res text/tokens.bin
$F4F5 b OtherTokens ; The other set's 263 strings (tools/tokens.py --set other): the missions, the planet descriptions, the commander menu
@res text/tokens.bin
$FC00 b TokensSpare 8 ; Eight zero bytes after the tables (known from the code only)
$FC08 b KeyScreens ; Keys down: ENTER 1, L 2, K 4, P 8, O $10, I $20, 0 $40 (the joystick's fire), Y $80 (the cloak)
$FC09 b KeySteer ; N 1 (roll left), M 2 (roll right), X 4 (climb), S 8 (dive), SPACE $10 (faster), SYMBOL SHIFT $20 (slower): the joystick's bits 0-3
$FC0A b KeyViews ; 1-4 bits 0-3 (the views, docked the launch and the trading screens), H $10 (hyperspace), G $20 (galactic), J $40 (the jump drive), CAPS SHIFT $80 (pause)
$FC0B b KeyCombat ; A 1 (fire), T 2 (target a missile), F 4 (fire the missile), U 8 (unarm), E $10 (E.C.M.), W $20 (energy bomb), Q $40 (escape pod), C $80 (docking computer)
$FC0C b KeyChart ; B $10 (the cursor home), D $20 (the distance), R $40 (a planet's name)
$FC0D b KeyCode ; The last key's character (KeyCodes); $FF none, $FE DELETE (CAPS SHIFT with 0)
$FC0E b Options ; The pause menu's options: bits 0-1 the controls (0 keyboard, 1 Kempston, 2 Cursor, 3 Sinclair), 2 recentring (R), 3 damping (D), 4 both axes reversed, 5 the vertical axis reversed, 6 the misjump (F), 7 sound
$FC0F b KeyDigits ; 9 1, 5 2, 8 4, 6 8, 7 $10: the Cursor and Sinclair joysticks' keys
$FC10 c ScanJoystick ; ScanKeyboard's row loop end; after the last row the joystick's four bits replace KeySteer's, reversed as the options say
> Kempston (port $1F): bit 4 the fire (KeyCombat bit 0), bits 0-3 the directions, the axes' reversal options inverted. Cursor: KeyDigits / 2 (5 left, 8 right, 6 down, 7 up). Sinclair: 6 left, 7 right, 8 down, 9 up. Both: the 0 key fires. Option bit 4 swaps left with right and down with up, bit 5 down with up. With the keyboard, a steering key held clears CAPS SHIFT, F and C (keys a matrix can ghost from N, M, X, S held together; the reason is not stated in the code). Finally 0 with CAPS SHIFT is DELETE ($FE in KeyCode). 13398 runs, the keyboard only.
$FC22 ScanJoystickKempston
$FC33 ScanJoystickKempstonBits
$FC3D ScanJoystickDigits
$FC57 ScanJoystickFire
$FC63 ScanJoystickReverse
$FC74 ScanJoystickVertical
$FC89 ScanJoystickStore
$FCA1 ScanJoystickSteer
$FCBA c KeyPressed ; Key E (bit 5 - E) of row D (8 the CAPS SHIFT row): its character into KeyCode, its bit into its key byte
> The index is bit x 8 + row - 1: KeyCodes gives the character, KeyTable two bytes (the offset from $FC08 and the mask). 1203 runs.
$FCD1 KeyPressedCode
$FCEA b VectorFiller 16 ; $FE bytes: what is left of a 257-byte IM2 table $FD00-$FE00 (the bytes past $FD00 still give $FEFE for a low bus byte)
$FD41 t KeyCodes 8 ; Each key's character by the index: SPACE, ENTER, P, 0, 1, Q, A, CAPS SHIFT (0), then the next bit of each row
$FD69 c ScanKeyboard ; The eight half-rows from $FEFE to $7FFE: every key down through KeyPressed; KeyDigits 0 and KeyCode $FF first
> 13398 runs (every interrupt of c1, f1, w1 and d1); 1203 keys seen down.
$FD76 ScanKeyboardRow
$FD80 ScanKeyboardBit
$FD8A b LaserItems 4 ; The equipment item of each laser kind 1-4 (5 pulse, 6 beam, 13 military, 14 mining): read at $FD89 + kind
$FD8E b StatusBands 8 ; The status page's colour bands (ColourBands: cells x 8 + rows, a row 0 ends)
$FD96 b InventoryBands 3 ; The inventory's
$FD99 t OtherPairs 26 ; The other set's 13 two-letter pairs (codes $D7 on); ControlRandomName uses those from $FD9B
$FDB3 t StdPairs 16 ; The standard set's 32 pairs (codes $80-$9F), also the system names' syllables: AL LE XE GE ZA CE BI SO US ES AR MA IN DI RE A? ER AT EN BE RA LA VE TI ED OR QU AN TE IS RI ON, as BBC Elite's
$FDF3 b DataBands 8 ; The data screen's colour bands
$FDFB b MarketBands2 3 ; The market prices' colour bands
$FDFE b VectorByte ; $FE (the filler's last byte)
$FDFF w IM2Vector ; $FEFE: the IM2 vector for the bus byte $FF (I = $FD), the handler's JR at $FEFE
$FE01 c ReadControls ; In a space view: the steering bits into the accumulators RollControl (N, M), PitchControl (X, S), SpeedControl (SPACE, SYMBOL SHIFT); KeySteer cleared
> The roll and the pitch are sign and magnitude words (bit 15 the sign): a key in the word's direction adds $FF (roll) or $66 (pitch) a frame up to a magnitude below $1000, a key against it takes as much off (with recentring, option bit 2: straight to 0), and with neither key the magnitude falls by $3C or $24 a frame (damping, option bit 3). The speed goes up $A0 a frame with SPACE (below $2000) and down with SYMBOL SHIFT (to 0). 13398 runs, 11035 in a space view.
$FE2E ReadControlsRight
$FE3A ReadControlsRightMore
$FE41 ReadControlsLeft
$FE51 ReadControlsLeftMore
$FE55 ReadControlsRollUp
$FE63 ReadControlsRollDown
$FE6D ReadControlsRollLess
$FE7A ReadControlsPitch
$FE9C ReadControlsClimb
$FEA8 ReadControlsClimbMore
$FEAF ReadControlsDive
$FEBF ReadControlsDiveMore
$FEC3 ReadControlsPitchUp
$FED1 ReadControlsPitchDown
$FEDB ReadControlsPitchLess
$FEE8 ReadControlsSpeed
$FEFE c IM2Entry ; The address the vector gives: JR IM2Handler
$FF00 ReadControlsFaster
$FF08 w RollControl ; The roll accumulator (sign and magnitude): its high byte $FF09 is the roll rate CopyRates takes
$FF0A w PitchControl ; The pitch accumulator, the rate in $FF0B
$FF0C w SpeedControl ; The speed accumulator, the speed in $FF0D
$FF0E ReadControlsSlower
$FF16 ReadControlsFasterCap
$FF1D ReadControlsDone
$FF25 c IM2Handler ; The interrupt: its own stack below $FFBF, the registers saved, ScanKeyboard, ReadControls and the sound (SoundTickVector)
> 13398 runs: one a frame. SP is kept in IM2SavedSP.
$FF4C c IM2On ; I = $FD, IM 2 (known from the code only: it ran before the recordings started)
$FF53 c IM1On ; IM 1 (for the tape routines in the ROM; known from the code only)
$FF56 w IM2SavedSP ; The interrupted program's SP
$FF58 b KeyTable 2 ; Each key's (offset from $FC08, mask) by the index; Z and V have the mask 0
